  "verbalization": "Certonardosterol E3 is shown to have a target relationship with Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including [(3aR,4S,6R,6aR,9aR,9bR)-6-hydroxy-6,9-dimethyl-3-methylidene-2-oxo-4,5,6a,7,9a,9b-hexahydro-3aH-azuleno[4,5-b]furan-4-yl] (E)-2-methylbut-2-enoate and [(1S,4aR,7aS)-7-hydroxy-7-methyl-1-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxy-4a,5,6,7a-tetrahydro-1H-cyclopenta[c]pyran-5-yl] 4-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzoate, both of which target HaCaT. This suggests that Certonardosterol E3 may exert its effects through a mechanism involving Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a key component in cellular processes such as microtubule dynamics and cell cycle regulation. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same protein indicates that the interaction may be mediated through a common pathway, possibly involving the modulation of microtubule-associated processes. The evidence supports a potential role for Certonardosterol E3 in influencing HaCaT cells through the regulation of microtubule-associated proteins, though further investigation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the extent of its biological impact.",
